  "answer": "No past ticket reports this exact problem. The new ticket says LocalKeyboardListener handles HC_NOREMOVE peek notifications as key events, so shortcuts can fire twice, and proposes processing only HC_ACTION. PowerToys#48725 is the closest, since it also describes a shortcut running twice (the context-item RequestedShortcut navigates twice). That ticket traces the cause to TryCommandKeybindingMessage being handled by both CommandBar and ContextMenu, not to the keyboard hook, so it is a different problem. This ticket should be triaged as new. The reporter could add reproduction steps, a specific shortcut that fires twice, and the expected and actual behavior."
 },
